# Shortest path through a maze, the shape a great many Advent of Code days take.
#
# `dijkstra` wants one thing: a function from a place to the (cost, place)
# steps leading out of it. Everything else — the frontier, the visited set, the
# order things come off — is its business, and what comes back is the cost of
# reaching every square the walker could get to, so a second question about the
# same maze costs nothing.
sheet is Source through pattern

cellAt k is cell sheet k else '#'

isOpen k is neq '#' (cellAt k)

findMark m is
  sheet through knots through seek (k gives eq m (cellAt k)) else knot 0 0

# Every open neighbour is one step away.
steps k is around4 sheet k where isOpen as (1, this)

reachable is dijkstra steps (findMark 'S')

get reachable (findMark 'E') else neg 1
